  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    Belts are the classic “one more item” spreadsheet add-on—cheap in ¥, small in the box—until a mis-engraved buckle ships or your freight line rejects trademark leather entirely.
    This guide maps the <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> <code>belts</code> pool as of <strong>30 June 2026</strong>: <strong>30 rows</strong> behind the homepage <a href="/category/accessories/">Accessories</a> shortcut, with overlap into <code>jewelry-watches</code> when sellers mis-tag cardholders.
  </p>

  <h2>June 2026 belts snapshot</h2>
  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">Belts lane</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Deep-lane rows (<code>belts</code>)</td><td>30</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Top labels (2 rows each)</td><td>Amiri, Burberry, Chrome Hearts, Dior, Fendi, Givenchy, Goyard, Gucci</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Homepage shortcut</td><td><a href="/category/accessories/">Accessories</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Counts come from our on-site English catalogue export. Brand strings describe seller metadata—not authorised distribution.
    For wider small leather context see <a href="/blog/kakobuy-accessories-spreadsheet-lane-guide-2026/">accessories overview</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What shoppers actually browse</h2>
  <h3>Luxury buckles (Dior, Gucci, Goyard, Fendi)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Dior</strong>, <strong>Gucci</strong>, <strong>Goyard</strong>, and <strong>Fendi</strong> belts recur in our snapshot—macro QC on buckle engravings, leather grain, and hole spacing is essential.
    These SKUs trigger <a href="/blog/shipping-branded-vs-unbranded-spreadsheet-restrictions/">branded shipping</a> scrutiny even when the item price looks trivial.
  </p>
  <h3>Streetwear &amp; statement (Chrome Hearts, Amiri)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Chrome Hearts</strong> and <strong>Amiri</strong> rows emphasise hardware weight and logo density—compare warehouse stills to listing close-ups, not distant mannequin shots.
  </p>
  <h3>Heritage check (Burberry, Givenchy)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Burberry</strong> check belts and <strong>Givenchy</strong> logo bands need pattern alignment across the strap length.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist for belt rows</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Buckle:</strong> engraving depth, font accuracy, plating colour.</li>
    <li><strong>Leather:</strong> grain consistency, edge paint, stamp placement.</li>
    <li><strong>Length &amp; holes:</strong> confirm size variant matches your order.</li>
    <li><strong>Packaging:</strong> box and dust bag if listing promises them.</li>
    <li><strong>Interior stamp:</strong> heat-stamp clarity and spacing.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Deep-read <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">warehouse QC</a>—belts are easy retake items when buckles fail macro inspection.
  </p>

  <h2>Freight &amp; consolidation notes</h2>
  <p>
    Belts ship light but can still complicate branded outbound carts mixed with bags or sneakers.
    Use <a href="/blog/kakobuy-rehearsal-packaging-freight/">rehearsal packaging</a> when belts tip a carton into a higher bracket.
  </p>

  <h2>Browse workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet home</a></strong> → <a href="/category/accessories/">Accessories</a> → <code>belts</code> pool.</li>
    <li>Copy live marketplace URLs—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-links-discovery-url-hygiene/">URL hygiene</a>.</li>
    <li>Freeze buckle colour and strap length variants.</li>
    <li>Approve QC on buckle macros—not seller renders.</li>
    <li>Quote branded-safe outbound lines before freight payment.</li>
  </ol>
